@law_won
title: The bill passes

= [+ law_name +]: passed

Yes [+ law_yes +], no [+ law_no +], abstentions [+ law_abstain +]. The vote is carried.[? if law_senate_delay = 1 : The government has no majority in the Senate, which vetoes the bill: Congress can lift the veto only in two months, and the law takes effect then. ?]

{!<div class="sp-last-vote"></div>!}
[? if law_partner_split = 1 : A coalition partner voted against, and the cracks are on every front page. ?]

@law_lost
title: The bill falls

= [+ law_name +]: defeated

{!<div class="sp-last-vote"></div>!}

Yes [+ law_yes +], no [+ law_no +], abstentions [+ law_abstain +]. The government loses a vote in its own Congress. It is not fatal, but it is noted.[? if law_partner_split = 1 : A coalition partner voted against, and the cracks are on every front page. ?]

@dare
title: A popular bill
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_national
view-if: player_in_government = 0 and sanchez_leader = 1 and law_timer <= 0

= Dare them to vote it down

From opposition, the PSOE can table a popular bill: a rise in the minimum wage, rent relief, a pensions guarantee. If it passes, you set the agenda. If the government kills it, they own the refusal.

- @dare_go: Table the bill
- @root: Not now

@dare_go
title: The bill is tabled
on-arrival: {! Q.month_actions += 1; Q.law_timer = 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.dareBill(Q); } !}

= The vote on the PSOE bill

[? if dare_passed = 1 : The opposition parties combine and the bill passes. The government is outvoted on its own floor. ?][? if dare_passed = 0 : The governing majority votes it down. Your bill fails, but now they have to explain why. ?]
